course: dictionary
lesson: 11251
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. Those words are its context, and they give you clues. «Worship» is one of these words.
explain: In RE lessons you learn how people worship: by praying, singing or going to services in a church, mosque, synagogue, temple or gurdwara. «The Sabbath is a day of rest and worship.» Here worship means religious acts of prayer and praise.
explain: Fans can also worship a pop star or footballer. That means they love and admire them very much. The clue is who is being worshipped: a person, not God. «Hero worship» is the phrase for this kind of strong admiration.
fact: Worship means to show love and respect to God or a god, by praying, singing or going to religious services.
fact: Worship as a noun means these acts of prayer and praise.
fact: A «place of worship» is a building where people pray, such as a church, mosque, synagogue, temple or gurdwara.
fact: «Worship» can also mean to love or admire someone very much, sometimes too much.
fact: «Quakers worship mostly in silence» means their worship is quiet, with little or no singing or speaking.
exercise: «Quakers worship mostly in silence.» What does worship mean here? | *Show love and respect to God by praying or being quiet together | Run races at school | Shout songs in the street | Cook a big meal for friends
exercise: Fans sing and cheer for their footballer and say they worship him. What does worship mean here? | To dance in a park | *To love or admire someone very much, sometimes too much | To pray to God in a church | To buy a new football
exercise: Which of these is a place of worship? | *A gurdwara | A supermarket | A library | A football pitch
test: «The Sabbath is a day of rest and worship.» In this sentence, worship means: | Shopping for food | Playing games with friends | *Acts of prayer and praise | Sleeping late in bed
test: Which phrase means very great admiration for a famous person? | Hero costume | Hero lunch | Hero jump | *Hero worship
exam: Sofia says worship always means going to church. Is she right? | *No, worship can mean religious acts in many places, or loving someone very much | No, worship is a type of food | Yes, but only on Sundays | Yes, worship only ever happens in churches
